Description: libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi: retarget the VAAPI device from SCALEPLEX_RENDER_DEVICE
 In a distributed scaleplex transcode worker the GPU lives on a different
 node than PMS, so the DRM render-node path Plex bakes into its
 `-init_hw_device vaapi=vaapi:<path>` argv (the PMS host's
 HardwareDevicePath) does not resolve on the worker. Until now the Go
 rewriter overwrote that path on every spawn.
 .
 This moves device retargeting into the binary: vaapi_device_create reads
 SCALEPLEX_RENDER_DEVICE and, when set, ignores whatever path the caller
 passed and binds that node instead. An empty caller path
 (`vaapi=vaapi:`) with no env set falls through to stock auto-detection
 (renderD128..) rather than failing on open(""). The `,driver=` opt and
 LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME continue to select the VA driver unchanged.
 .
 Effect: any caller's argv lands on the worker's GPU without rewriter
 intervention, shrinking the rewriter toward a drop-in transcoder.
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-24
---
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #if HAVE_UNISTD_H
 #   include <unistd.h>
 #endif
@@ -1699,6 +1700,22 @@
     const AVDictionaryEntry *ent;
     int try_drm, try_x11, try_win32, try_all;
 
+    /* scaleplex: in a distributed transcode worker the GPU lives on a
+     * different node than PMS, so the DRM path Plex bakes into
+     * -init_hw_device (its host's HardwareDevicePath) does not resolve
+     * here. When SCALEPLEX_RENDER_DEVICE is set, ignore the caller's
+     * path and bind the worker's GPU; an empty caller path
+     * ("vaapi=vaapi:") falls back to stock auto-detection rather than
+     * open(""). Moves device retargeting out of the scaleplex Go
+     * rewriter into the binary. */
+    {
+        const char *sp_dev = getenv("SCALEPLEX_RENDER_DEVICE");
+        if (sp_dev && *sp_dev)
+            device = sp_dev;
+        else if (device && !*device)
+            device = NULL;
+    }
+
     priv = av_mallocz(sizeof(*priv));
     if (!priv)
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
